; Every way of writing something which is not an id. Each names the rule it
; broke rather than only that it broke one, because "invalid id" leaves the
; author to work out which half of the production they missed.

; No colon at all, which is a local part with no authority behind it.
(node S-101
  (kind Space)
  (type MeetingRoom)
  (geometry area))

; A colon with nothing in front of it.
(node :S-102
  (kind Space)
  (type MeetingRoom)
  (geometry area))

; A colon with nothing after it.
(node site:
  (kind Space)
  (type MeetingRoom)
  (geometry area))

; A namespace beginning with a digit is not written here because it cannot be:
; a lexeme beginning with a digit is a number attempt to the tokenizer, so
; `3d:S-104` is a lexical error reported before any of this is consulted, and
; one which would take the rest of the file down with it. Confining a namespace
; to ASCII beginning with a letter is what keeps that from being the diagnostic
; anybody sees.

; Punctuation a symbol permits and a namespace does not.
(node site.local:S-105
  (kind Space)
  (type MeetingRoom)
  (geometry area))
